      "name": "visualizer-loading",
      "title": "Visualizer loading — the page is layout, the graph is fetched",
      "description": "The general strategy for a complex visualizer: the generated page carries identity, layout and a pointer, and its bulky or repeated content is fetched from the Knowledge Graph in the browser rather than baked into every page. What must stay server-side, how to fetch, how to stay equivalent to the render being replaced, and how to verify a page whose content is not in its HTML. Read before generating any page that shows a KG node's data at length: an IG artefact view, a graph viewer, a schema or sidecar view.",
